  "retained_failures": [
    "Public direct KLayout changed-turn controls both reject; the initially suspected turn-count false pass was not reproduced.",
    "Native Netgen two-terminal L interpretation loses the substrate terminal; even nominal comparison fails.",
    "Early isolated coupons lost electrical port names to LA/LB role labels and had insufficient substrate contact enclosure.",
    "The public center-tap bridge has two vertices 10 nm off 45 degrees; the explicit corrected coupon and original mask are both retained.",
    "Decorative multiline text was silently replaced in OASIS; export now refuses unsupported text before touching its destination.",
    "Full v4 batch passed 35/36 checks: an interturn bridge bypassed a coil turn but public DRC and native parameter comparison still passed. The final topology check rejects it.",
    "The first archive attempt rejected duplicate manifest names; the separately verified v3 archive is the bound recovery source.",
    "The stricter v6 fault gate did not recognize Netgen's failed-pin-matching diagnostic in two controls. The final gate accepts that explicit finding while rejecting crashed tools and missing evidence; v7 passes all 36 cases."
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Physical L records become explicit X comparison primitives preserving every terminal and W/S/D/NR_R/M.",
    "Private source-checked extraction corrections preserve recognition text and assign LA/LC/LB roles independently of rotation without global electrical names.",
    "Actual TopMetal1/TopVia2/TopMetal2 connectivity and conductive-loop checking precede public device recognition.",
    "OASIS refuses lossy text substitution; generic GDS remains available.",
    "Both source editor formats and native 36-case CI regression are added."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "IHP coil electrical models remain unavailable; catalog status is unchanged.",
    "Two fixed geometry fixtures do not qualify the continuous winding parameter range or filled/slotted windings.",
    "Public derived D differs by 10 nm from the center-tap fixture horizontal inner opening; both measurements are recorded.",
    "No inductance, Q, coupling, substrate loss, noise, RF calibration or fabrication signoff claim.",
    "Chunk 7 still requires missing model/family coverage, reviewed operating envelopes, full upstream view/option reconciliation and installed-runtime acceptance."
  ],
